WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:06.770
Fight for your justice,
show your courage.

00:06.770 --> 00:10.370
Right! Grasp truth in these hands.

00:10.370 --> 00:13.780
Fight for your justice, I want you

00:13.780 --> 00:21.200
as you fight through
with your head held up high.

00:35.860 --> 00:39.930
Rather than polishing diamonds

00:43.040 --> 00:46.970
give me a glistening future.

00:50.250 --> 00:52.480
Even if nothing's there, get up.

00:52.480 --> 00:56.350
It's important to turn on the switch.

00:57.450 --> 01:00.220
Something new that I don't want to yield.

01:00.220 --> 01:04.750
Seeking it is justice!

01:06.360 --> 01:09.930
Fight for your justice,
be serious about it.

01:09.930 --> 01:13.540
Right! Face reality head on.

01:13.540 --> 01:16.940
Fight for your justice,
I love how you

01:16.940 --> 01:27.340
never give up even if
the current is against you.

01:33.150 --> 01:35.920
Tarak fleet locked onto the Nirvana!

01:35.920 --> 01:39.380
Don't shoot! Please, I beg you...

01:42.930 --> 01:46.100
Mejale fleet confirmed
to be behind Tarak fleet!

01:46.100 --> 01:48.500
Both fleets ready to attack!

01:48.500 --> 01:49.640
Attack?

01:49.640 --> 01:51.770
Are you saying we're their enemy?

01:51.770 --> 01:53.780
Something's going on...

01:53.780 --> 01:56.610
We have word from the Tarak fleet.

01:56.610 --> 02:00.180
"Female pirates,
surrender unconditionally now..."

02:00.180 --> 02:01.380
is what they say.

02:01.380 --> 02:03.350
Can't they talk directly to us?

02:03.350 --> 02:04.450
On Tarak

02:04.450 --> 02:08.290
they say their ears and voices
will rot if they speak to women.

02:08.290 --> 02:10.360
Stupid...

02:10.360 --> 02:12.730
The Mejale fleet is hailing us, as well!

02:12.730 --> 02:14.800
"If you follow Tarak's orders

02:14.800 --> 02:19.670
we will rendezvous now
and collect your crew," they say.

02:19.670 --> 02:23.770
It'd be best not
to stir things up for now.

02:23.770 --> 02:25.140
To not fight...

02:25.140 --> 02:27.210
That's all we have left now.

02:27.210 --> 02:30.710
How do you think Tarak
will react to all of this.

02:30.710 --> 02:32.850
The women living or dying depends

02:32.850 --> 02:36.180
on how the captain deals
with the harvest information.

02:36.180 --> 02:40.390
In other words, our ace is the harvest?

02:40.390 --> 02:43.480
No, we have one more ace in our hand.

02:59.370 --> 03:02.280
Women are monsters, or so they look.

03:06.510 --> 03:08.570
Stop it! You're going against a child!

03:12.220 --> 03:14.360
Let's see... Where was it?

03:14.360 --> 03:16.020
What are you doing, Dita?

03:16.020 --> 03:17.660
We have to hurry up.

03:17.660 --> 03:19.330
Yeah, just a second.

03:19.330 --> 03:21.320
This isn't the time...

03:23.870 --> 03:24.930
For Hibiki?

03:24.930 --> 03:28.440
And for the doctor,
the pilot, and the vice-captain.

03:28.440 --> 03:30.410
- The vice-captain?
- Yeah!

03:30.410 --> 03:34.440
They're going back to that
horrible-tasting food again, right?

03:34.440 --> 03:37.410
So I thought of a yummy menu,
even when cold!

03:37.410 --> 03:39.740
Do you understand the situation?

03:50.830 --> 03:51.830
My, my.

03:51.830 --> 03:54.960
What an extravagant escort we have.

03:54.960 --> 03:58.400
Then I guess I'll accept the invitation.

03:59.870 --> 04:00.840
Done!

04:00.840 --> 04:02.640
Come on, let's hurry!

04:02.640 --> 04:05.440
Hey, hurry up!

04:05.440 --> 04:07.100
Dita!

04:08.810 --> 04:10.470
Handcuffs?

04:13.150 --> 04:16.380
Come to think of it,
this is a curious twist of fate.

04:16.380 --> 04:20.360
This was where you met Dita, right?

04:20.360 --> 04:24.230
And this ship was where we all first met.

04:24.230 --> 04:27.230
We found out about men here...

04:27.230 --> 04:28.630
And women...

04:28.630 --> 04:31.300
And the truth about
a world yet to come...

04:31.300 --> 04:34.400
Hey, what are you scheming up?

04:34.400 --> 04:38.770
I don't like how normally
noisy guys are being quiet.

04:38.770 --> 04:40.070
Don't worry.

04:40.070 --> 04:43.140
Bart's been like this
since the vice-captain.

04:43.140 --> 04:45.950
And being apart from
Kahlua is hard on Pyoro.

04:45.950 --> 04:49.580
Hey, you found out I'm from
the first generation, right?

04:49.580 --> 04:52.220
Yes, it seems so.

04:52.220 --> 04:54.360
Then leave it to me!

04:54.360 --> 04:55.690
I'll talk it out!

04:55.690 --> 04:57.590
Oh, interesting...

04:57.590 --> 04:59.990
That would be the most peaceful way.

04:59.990 --> 05:03.160
You see? I'll talk to gramps first

05:03.160 --> 05:05.370
then the seven other geezers.

05:05.370 --> 05:07.630
I'll talk and that'll be it...!

05:13.470 --> 05:15.140
What...

05:19.110 --> 05:20.210
Swallowed up?

05:20.210 --> 05:22.820
The Paksis is keeping him safe.

05:22.820 --> 05:24.690
I see...

05:24.690 --> 05:27.920
Hibiki is one who shouldn't
be here in the first place.

05:27.920 --> 05:30.990
Therefore, he will
serve as the ace in our hand.

05:30.990 --> 05:33.630
How'd you come up with that?

05:33.630 --> 05:35.260
Thanks to the vice-captain.

05:35.260 --> 05:38.870
That's taboo to say in front of me...

05:38.870 --> 05:40.740
What should I do?

05:40.740 --> 05:43.000
You just lie around and play dead!

05:43.000 --> 05:45.340
You're digging into my temple!

05:49.010 --> 05:50.480
Barnette, hurry!

05:50.480 --> 05:53.680
I know. Just a bit longer.

05:53.680 --> 05:55.050
What's that?

05:55.050 --> 05:57.750
These? They're all one-of-a-kind items.

05:57.750 --> 06:00.320
No, I meant that book.

06:00.320 --> 06:01.690
Oh...

06:01.690 --> 06:04.990
I thought I would need this...

06:04.990 --> 06:06.690
You're still hung up on that?

06:06.690 --> 06:08.900
Before that, what are you doing?

06:08.900 --> 06:10.000
Security.

06:10.000 --> 06:12.900
So we don't let them
have free access to this ship.

06:15.270 --> 06:16.940
What's with those outfits?

06:16.940 --> 06:19.270
It's too much and not stylish...

06:19.270 --> 06:20.930
That hurts!

06:29.780 --> 06:31.890
- I'm saved!
- It's all right!

06:31.890 --> 06:33.690
They didn't eat your liver yet?

06:33.690 --> 06:35.680
They had enough food.

06:41.360 --> 06:43.020
Good work, sir.

06:46.570 --> 06:48.260
The prime minister is waiting.

06:51.340 --> 06:53.360
That was Bart, wasn't it...

07:11.530 --> 07:12.830
How horrible!

07:12.830 --> 07:15.730
W-Why?

07:15.730 --> 07:17.230
Throw this thing away!

07:17.230 --> 07:18.430
"Hello, Baby"

07:18.430 --> 07:20.330
"Hello, Baby"
Burn it immediately!

07:20.330 --> 07:21.840
"Hello, Baby"
Yes, ma'am!

07:21.840 --> 07:22.270
Yes, ma'am!

07:22.270 --> 07:24.140
Are you kidding? Give it back!

07:24.140 --> 07:26.230
Quiet, Ms. Elden!

07:28.680 --> 07:34.620
Would you drag others down
a sinful path with this publication?

07:34.620 --> 07:35.780
Huh?

07:35.780 --> 07:38.550
Ms. Elden, you are a witch!

07:38.550 --> 07:40.250
No, not just you.

07:40.250 --> 07:44.230
Magno's pirates are nothing
more than despicable witches!

07:44.230 --> 07:47.430
Witch? Who are you calling a witch?

07:47.430 --> 07:49.230
I've heard about this...

07:49.230 --> 07:51.390
but Mejale really is something else.

07:52.400 --> 07:54.040
From what I hear

07:54.040 --> 07:57.570
you've spreaded an
unfounded rumor of a "harvest."

07:57.570 --> 08:02.380
And you were using that
as part of a pirate coup d'etat.

08:02.380 --> 08:04.010
A coup d'etat?

08:04.010 --> 08:06.050
Talk about playing the victim.

08:06.050 --> 08:10.750
Oh? We didn't know that, either.

08:10.750 --> 08:14.620
These people haven't been
informed about the harvest.

08:17.530 --> 08:20.430
In Grand Ma's name,
I now give my verdict!

08:20.430 --> 08:23.500
Magno Vivan and crew
are sentenced for life.

08:23.500 --> 08:26.870
Transport them to
the purgatorial area now.

08:26.870 --> 08:28.530
That is all.

08:33.610 --> 08:36.780
It's all right... It's all right, Kahlua.

08:36.780 --> 08:38.770
This court is now adjourned.

08:41.020 --> 08:42.520
You don't get it at all!

08:42.520 --> 08:45.120
Hey, quiet!

08:45.120 --> 08:48.460
You don't even try
to see if what we say is true!

08:48.460 --> 08:51.360
And you keep the
truth away from everyone!

08:51.360 --> 08:54.200
Why aren't you trying to listen to us?

08:54.200 --> 08:56.730
It's not an unfounded rumor!

08:56.730 --> 08:59.570
The harvest is right around the corner!

08:59.570 --> 09:03.770
If you keep measuring with an old ruler,
you'll stay blind forever!

09:03.770 --> 09:05.430
Dita...

09:08.610 --> 09:10.270
We're adjourned.

09:25.790 --> 09:28.000
That was really cool, Dita.

09:28.000 --> 09:31.260
Our trip wasn't a mistake, right?

09:33.800 --> 09:35.460
I'm sure of it.

09:41.980 --> 09:45.910
The information about
Mejale that you have told us

09:45.910 --> 09:50.990
will most likely be of value
in our future dealings against them.

09:50.990 --> 09:56.420
Grand Pa was very happy about it.

09:56.420 --> 09:58.890
Thank you very much.

10:01.560 --> 10:04.500
Couldn't something be done with...
you know.

10:04.500 --> 10:07.500
Unless the order that
my mission is completed...

10:07.500 --> 10:10.710
In other words,
I am waiting for your orders, sir.

10:10.710 --> 10:12.700
Do you not like this appearance?

10:23.580 --> 10:26.790
We will now
re-educate Garsus and McFile.

10:26.790 --> 10:31.950
The way they talk suggests
they wish to co-habitate with women.

10:34.030 --> 10:39.090
That is something that should
not be in a proud man of Tarak.

10:59.950 --> 11:03.360
- Thank you.
- I'll hold her anytime.

11:03.360 --> 11:04.950
Just tell me if you get too tired.

11:06.260 --> 11:08.260
I'm not finished yet.

11:08.260 --> 11:11.830
I don't know why I was awakened.

11:11.830 --> 11:13.490
Are you scared?

11:15.070 --> 11:16.470
No.

11:16.470 --> 11:18.710
Don't think about it too much.

11:18.710 --> 11:22.210
It's one of your bad habits.

11:22.210 --> 11:24.710
I...

11:24.710 --> 11:30.050
I was thinking about what Hibiki
would say in a situation like this.

11:32.050 --> 11:35.860
The same thing you would say.

11:35.860 --> 11:37.520
Yes...

12:02.520 --> 12:04.690
Y-You're...

12:04.690 --> 12:07.290
Magno Vivan, right?

12:07.290 --> 12:08.960
I-It is you!

12:08.960 --> 12:10.260
Really?

12:10.260 --> 12:12.130
Magno Vivan? The pirate?

12:12.130 --> 12:14.130
Someone amazing's here!

12:14.130 --> 12:15.200
She's so cool!

12:15.200 --> 12:18.800
You came here to save us, right?

12:18.800 --> 12:20.600
- My...
- Shut up! Shut up!

12:20.600 --> 12:21.840
Quiet down!

12:21.840 --> 12:23.140
What is this?

12:23.140 --> 12:24.170
Dunno...

12:24.170 --> 12:26.810
Oh, so you guys are all famous...

12:26.810 --> 12:27.810
That's right!

12:27.810 --> 12:29.810
We're carefree pirates!

12:29.810 --> 12:31.680
We always have to have fun!

12:31.680 --> 12:34.420
This is a fun situation?

12:34.420 --> 12:36.520
We win if we have fun with it.

12:36.520 --> 12:38.590
Hey, let us join you!

12:38.590 --> 12:40.120
Me, too!

12:40.120 --> 12:41.920
Let me in, too!

12:41.920 --> 12:44.230
Can you hear this, Mr. Alien?

12:44.230 --> 12:48.130
People who want to change
this world and themselves...

12:48.130 --> 12:50.430
There are so many here, too!

12:52.670 --> 12:54.200
H-Huh?

12:54.200 --> 12:56.200
What's going on here?

12:56.200 --> 12:59.040
Ow... They framed me!

13:04.810 --> 13:06.080
I know.

13:06.080 --> 13:08.650
They're coming soon, right?

13:08.650 --> 13:11.520
But there's no need to tremble in fear...

13:11.520 --> 13:13.610
I'm not going to lose!

13:43.420 --> 13:45.890
Everyone's been transported.

13:45.890 --> 13:47.690
Is it just you?

13:47.690 --> 13:50.360
I'm baby-sitting.

13:50.360 --> 13:51.760
They're coming.

13:51.760 --> 13:53.560
I feel it, too.

13:53.560 --> 13:55.460
Then we'll go by ourselves!

13:55.460 --> 13:59.070
Barnette put a security
code on the Nirvana!

13:59.070 --> 14:02.140
Men can't move it themselves.

14:02.140 --> 14:03.800
Damn her!

14:08.210 --> 14:10.510
Swear allegiance to Lord Grand Pa!

14:10.510 --> 14:12.750
Spit it out now!

14:12.750 --> 14:14.410
Damn you!

14:17.020 --> 14:18.250
It's useless...

14:18.250 --> 14:21.820
We won't change our ideals...

14:21.820 --> 14:23.590
Bart!

14:23.590 --> 14:27.060
If you're a man,
don't you want to save him?

14:27.060 --> 14:32.370
You two will be saved with one phrase,
"Hail Lord Grand Pa."

14:32.370 --> 14:35.400
You're what's called
victims of circumstance.

14:35.400 --> 14:36.700
Your head's numbed

14:36.700 --> 14:41.210
and you've been implanted with
an illusion of living with women.

14:41.210 --> 14:44.980
You're the victim of circumstance.

14:44.980 --> 14:47.210
Women are wonderful.

14:47.210 --> 14:51.290
I can relish life
because of my days with them.

14:51.290 --> 14:54.810
I'll show your body what
it really means to relish life!

15:05.570 --> 15:06.630
How are they?

15:06.630 --> 15:08.600
Persistent, sir.

15:08.600 --> 15:12.070
They're completely tainted by women.

15:12.070 --> 15:13.640
Throwing away those days

15:13.640 --> 15:15.910
for another medal of honor, eh?

15:19.380 --> 15:21.450
My feelings won't change.

15:21.450 --> 15:26.620
I fell in love with you
when you were a woman!

15:26.620 --> 15:28.890
Hand it over. I'll do it.

15:28.890 --> 15:30.550
Yes, sir.

15:33.490 --> 15:34.730
Now watch.

15:34.730 --> 15:38.130
This is how you use a whip!

15:45.370 --> 15:47.740
Let's go. Hibiki is waiting.

15:52.680 --> 15:57.820
Having something else bouncing
on my chest is quite annoying.

15:57.820 --> 15:59.550
Rather interesting.

16:03.090 --> 16:04.220
Enemy attack!

16:04.220 --> 16:06.490
Emergency battle setup! Hurry!

16:10.460 --> 16:12.800
Fight the intruders...

16:12.800 --> 16:14.030
Don't kill them.

16:14.030 --> 16:15.400
Just keep them down.

16:15.400 --> 16:17.060
Roger!

16:17.570 --> 16:20.710
Captain!

16:20.710 --> 16:22.680
We're here to pick you up.

16:22.680 --> 16:25.110
You're rather late.

16:25.110 --> 16:27.210
There was a lot of traffic.

16:27.210 --> 16:28.450
Who are they?

16:28.450 --> 16:30.580
The veterans from the hideout!

16:30.580 --> 16:32.920
Rebecca, you came for us!

16:32.920 --> 16:34.520
Ezra!

16:34.520 --> 16:35.720
That girl...

16:35.720 --> 16:38.390
Kahlua, meet your ohma!

16:42.830 --> 16:45.590
We'll let you all on our ship!

16:48.400 --> 16:50.870
What are BC and Gascogne doing?

16:50.870 --> 16:52.710
Leaving our captain like this...

16:52.710 --> 16:54.580
I'll tell stories later.

16:54.580 --> 16:57.640
There are plenty of
things we have to do first.

16:57.640 --> 16:59.310
Then let's go to the hideout...

16:59.310 --> 17:02.220
No, we'll take back the Nirvana now.

17:02.220 --> 17:04.320
The Nirvana?

17:04.320 --> 17:06.480
It's a place that's out of this world.

17:15.200 --> 17:16.960
It's moving, right?

17:16.960 --> 17:19.630
The Paksis is moving it.

17:19.630 --> 17:21.620
All right, now we can go!

17:23.900 --> 17:26.470
The Nirvana boots at the Paksis' will.

17:26.470 --> 17:30.440
Human-based systems
are at Barnette's will.

17:30.440 --> 17:33.380
Hurry up and get back here, idiot!

17:38.450 --> 17:39.490
Impossible!

17:39.490 --> 17:40.750
Who's moving the ship?

17:40.750 --> 17:43.560
Female pirates approaching the Ikazuchi!

17:43.560 --> 17:46.190
Captain, pirates!

17:46.190 --> 17:47.190
Shall we attack?

17:47.190 --> 17:48.360
Hold on.

17:48.360 --> 17:52.900
If Lord Grand Pa's Ikazuchi gets
even one scratch, my head will fly.

17:52.900 --> 17:54.890
Just continue pursuit!

17:59.710 --> 18:02.940
Welcome back!

18:02.940 --> 18:03.980
Mr. Alien!

18:03.980 --> 18:05.780
Hey.

18:05.780 --> 18:09.120
Y-You shouldn't eat that.

18:09.120 --> 18:11.390
You can't fight on an empty stomach.

18:11.390 --> 18:14.490
Besides, this was
pretty good even when cold.

18:14.490 --> 18:16.120
Mr. Alien...

18:16.120 --> 18:19.290
Hold on, I'll make
something warmer and yummier.

18:19.290 --> 18:21.060
Geez, what is that?

18:21.060 --> 18:22.030
Pyoro-2!

18:22.030 --> 18:23.260
Hey!

18:23.260 --> 18:25.030
Pyoro-2!

18:25.030 --> 18:26.900
W-What is this thing?

18:26.900 --> 18:29.340
- Who are you?
- What are you?

18:29.340 --> 18:31.670
I'm Pyoro-2's father!

18:31.670 --> 18:36.140
- What's Pyoro-2?
- Pyoro-2 is my baby!

18:36.140 --> 18:37.680
Hey, old hag.

18:37.680 --> 18:39.510
Finally time to show up, huh?

18:39.510 --> 18:41.820
I was rather tied up...

18:41.820 --> 18:43.480
Yeah, tell me about it!

18:43.480 --> 18:47.390
I'm not even from Mejale,
and they put me in prison!

18:47.390 --> 18:49.220
I have a record now.

18:49.220 --> 18:52.630
Whatever, just hurry
and unlock the security code!

18:52.630 --> 18:54.030
We can't do a thing!

18:54.030 --> 18:55.000
Oh?

18:55.000 --> 18:58.560
The password is a word
that both you and I know...

19:00.500 --> 19:02.090
Look.

19:04.200 --> 19:05.510
See?

19:05.510 --> 19:07.270
What the hell...

19:07.270 --> 19:09.370
There's no time to sulk.

19:10.410 --> 19:13.250
Let's go. Ready?

19:13.250 --> 19:14.240
Yeah!

19:21.160 --> 19:22.920
Let's get on with it now!

19:22.920 --> 19:26.160
A pod is approaching from Tarak!
Shall we intercept?

19:26.160 --> 19:28.600
It won't begin unless we do, right?

19:28.600 --> 19:30.590
Sorry to keep you waiting!

19:32.170 --> 19:35.360
Bart Garsus, here at your call!

19:37.300 --> 19:39.010
You're late!

19:39.010 --> 19:42.410
Don't waste time. Get into position.

19:42.410 --> 19:44.070
Roger that!

19:48.980 --> 19:51.080
How long will you stand there?

19:54.390 --> 19:58.880
You're not thinking of sneaking
off by any chance, are you?

20:01.400 --> 20:05.500
I don't recall revoking
your position as vice-captain.

20:05.500 --> 20:09.240
T-Then are you going to forgive me?

20:09.240 --> 20:11.000
Forgive or not...

20:11.000 --> 20:15.780
you came back here as Buzam, right?

20:15.780 --> 20:17.240
Thank you so much!

20:17.240 --> 20:18.810
But!

20:18.810 --> 20:20.580
I have one condition!

20:23.380 --> 20:28.190
Can you go back to
the voice you used before?

20:28.190 --> 20:29.850
Understood.

20:32.530 --> 20:34.690
Orders, Vice-captain?

20:39.130 --> 20:41.370
Attention, all Nirvana crew.

20:41.370 --> 20:44.040
All ships, prepare for battle!

20:44.040 --> 20:46.970
All others, stay at level 3 status.

20:46.970 --> 20:49.810
Bart, set a course for 5-3-8!

20:49.810 --> 20:51.210
Roger that!

20:51.210 --> 20:54.280
Ezra, status report on the Nirvana.

20:54.280 --> 20:55.280
Right!

20:55.280 --> 20:57.350
Cel, open a line with Rebecca.

20:57.350 --> 20:59.010
Right!

21:02.920 --> 21:04.630
Everyone, listen up!

21:04.630 --> 21:07.730
No matter how we struggle
or how painful it gets

21:07.730 --> 21:12.000
don't even think of ending it all
easily by dying! That's nonsense!

21:12.000 --> 21:18.560
A bright, exciting, and
cruel future awaits you all!

21:20.170 --> 21:22.870
Still the same old hag with a bad mouth.
